Manage the named IAM policies, attach them to users and groups and simulate their
effect. The built-in policies are readonly, readwrite, writeonly, diagnostics and
consoleAdmin.

Usage:
  nexoctl admin policy [flags]
  nexoctl admin policy [command]

Available Commands:
  attach      Attach policies to a user or a group
  create      Create a policy from a JSON document (FILE, or - for stdin)
  detach      Detach policies from a user or a group
  entities    List the users and groups a policy is attached to
  info        Print the document of a policy
  list        List the policies
  remove      Remove policies (built-in policies cannot be removed)
  simulate    Simulate a request: allowed or denied, and by which statement
  validate    Validate a policy document without saving it

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for policy

Global Flags:
      --config-dir string   configuration directory (default $NEXOCTL_CONFIG_DIR or ~/.nexoctl)
      --debug               dump the HTTP requests and responses on stderr, with the secrets redacted
      --json                print JSON Lines (one object per line with a "status" member)
      --no-color            disable colors (also with the NO_COLOR environment variable)
  -q, --quiet               hide confirmations and progress (results and errors are still printed)

Use "nexoctl admin policy [command] --help" for more information about a command.
